{"content_hash": "a6cd7b03fe069b10", "version_id": 429, "article_id": 43, "level_code": "ja_n2", "lang": "ja", "level": 4, "level_label": "N2 中高級", "title": "NHS待機リストが2か月連続で増加、冬の圧力に「不吉な兆候」", "title_zh": "NHS等待名单连续两个月增加，冬季压力出现“不祥信号”", "has_translation": true, "topic": "health", "source": "bbc_health", "source_url": "https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cxnv03e9nmp4o?at_medium=RSS&at_campaign=rss", "image": {"type": "photo", "url": "https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1540683153640-c28d7f6810f0?ixid=M3wxMDk3Mzk1fDB8MXxzZWFyY2h8N3x8b21pbm91cyUyMHNpZ25zJTIwd2ludGVyfGVufDB8MHx8fDE3OTE1OTQ0Mzd8MA&ixlib=rb-4.1.0&w=1600&q=75&fm=jpg&fit=max", "provider": "unsplash", "credit": "Photo by Shawn Bagley on Unsplash", "author": "Shawn Bagley", "credit_url": "https://unsplash.com/@utahdesertguy?utm_source=daily-english-news&utm_medium=referral", "source": "Unsplash", "source_url": "https://unsplash.com/photos/road-sign-near-pine-trees-bUADDFi1Qs0?utm_source=daily-english-news&utm_medium=referral", "fallback": {"type": "gradient", "from": "hsl(352, 42%, 62%)", "to": "hsl(30, 46%, 48%)", "label": "HEALTH", "seed": "b128cdf1738d"}}, "published_date": "2026-10-08", "word_count": 267, "reading_minutes": 0.9, "lead": "イングランドのNHSで、病院の待機リストが2か月連続で増加した。医療指導者らは、冬の圧力がすでに始まっているとして警告を発している。", "lead_zh": "英格兰NHS的医院等待名单连续两个月增加。医疗负责人警告说，冬季压力已经开始显现。", "preview": "8月末時点で、624万人の患者に関わる737万件の治療が実施を待っていた。これは2025年10月以来の最高水準であり、政府が2029年までに患者の92％を18週間以内に治療するという目標を達成できるか疑問視されている。", "preview_zh": "截至8月底，有624万名患者相关的737万项治疗等待实施。这是2025年10月以来的最高水平，政府能否在2029年前实现92%的患者在18周内得到治疗的目标受到质疑。", "has_audio": true, "audio": {"id": 419, "url": "https://pub-aba43a6fb1db4dc08fede1dbc81f3241.r2.dev/audio/43/ja_n2.mp3", "duration": 60.625, "size_bytes": 367488, "engine": "edge-tts", "voice": "ja-JP-NanamiNeural", "word_count": 183, "has_timeline": true}, "detail_url": "https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/chjam12301-sys/news-etl@fc48a26/content/data/versions/429.json", "paragraphs": ["8月末時点で、624万人の患者に関わる737万件の治療が実施を待っていた。これは2025年10月以来の最高水準であり、政府が2029年までに患者の92％を18週間以内に治療するという目標を達成できるか疑問視されている。", "待機リストの増加にもかかわらず、NHSは夏の間に記録的な数の計画手術を実施した。6月から8月にかけて470万件の治療や検査が行われ、過去最多となった。しかし、9月には救急部門と救急車サービスがともに記録的な数の患者を迎えた。", "NHSイングランドのフランキー・ソーズ国家医療部長は、スタッフがすでにインフルエンザや呼吸器ウイルスの患者の増加という「不吉な初期兆候」を目にしていると述べた。"], "paragraphs_zh": ["截至8月底，有624万名患者相关的737万项治疗等待实施。这是2025年10月以来的最高水平，政府能否在2029年前实现92%的患者在18周内得到治疗的目标受到质疑。", "尽管等待名单增加，NHS在夏季实施了创纪录数量的计划手术。6月至8月期间进行了470万项治疗和检查，为历史最多。然而9月份，急诊部门和救护车服务都接待了创纪录数量的患者。", "NHS英格兰国家医疗主任弗兰基·索兹表示，工作人员已经看到流感和其他呼吸道病毒患者增加这一“不祥的早期迹象”。她还指出，许多患者等待的时间比期望的要长。"], "body": "8月末時点で、624万人の患者に関わる737万件の治療が実施を待っていた。これは2025年10月以来の最高水準であり、政府が2029年までに患者の92％を18週間以内に治療するという目標を達成できるか疑問視されている。\n\n待機リストの増加にもかかわらず、NHSは夏の間に記録的な数の計画手術を実施した。6月から8月にかけて470万件の治療や検査が行われ、過去最多となった。しかし、9月には救急部門と救急車サービスがともに記録的な数の患者を迎えた。\n\nNHSイングランドのフランキー・ソーズ国家医療部長は、スタッフがすでにインフルエンザや呼吸器ウイルスの患者の増加という「不吉な初期兆候」を目にしていると述べた。", "body_zh": "截至8月底，有624万名患者相关的737万项治疗等待实施。这是2025年10月以来的最高水平，政府能否在2029年前实现92%的患者在18周内得到治疗的目标受到质疑。\n\n尽管等待名单增加，NHS在夏季实施了创纪录数量的计划手术。6月至8月期间进行了470万项治疗和检查，为历史最多。然而9月份，急诊部门和救护车服务都接待了创纪录数量的患者。\n\nNHS英格兰国家医疗主任弗兰基·索兹表示，工作人员已经看到流感和其他呼吸道病毒患者增加这一“不祥的早期迹象”。她还指出，许多患者等待的时间比期望的要长。", "text": "8月末時点で、624万人の患者に関わる737万件の治療が実施を待っていた。これは2025年10月以来の最高水準であり、政府が2029年までに患者の92％を18週間以内に治療するという目標を達成できるか疑問視されている。 待機リストの増加にもかかわらず、NHSは夏の間に記録的な数の計画手術を実施した。6月から8月にかけて470万件の治療や検査が行われ、過去最多となった。しかし、9月には救急部門と救急車サービスがともに記録的な数の患者を迎えた。 NHSイングランドのフランキー・ソーズ国家医療部長は、スタッフがすでにインフルエンザや呼吸器ウイルスの患者の増加という「不吉な初期兆候」を目にしていると述べた。", "vocab": [{"word": "待機リスト", "pos": "noun", "zh": "等待名单", "note": "医疗语境中常指等待治疗的患者名单"}, {"word": "増加", "pos": "noun", "zh": "增加", "note": "可作名词或サ变动词"}, {"word": "圧力", "pos": "noun", "zh": "压力", "note": "常与「かかる」「高まる」搭配"}, {"word": "兆候", "pos": "noun", "zh": "征兆、迹象", "note": "常与「不吉な」「初期の」搭配"}, {"word": "達成", "pos": "noun", "zh": "达成、实现", "note": "常与「目標」「公約」搭配"}, {"word": "記録的", "pos": "adj", "zh": "创纪录的", "note": "形容数量或程度空前"}, {"word": "救急部門", "pos": "noun", "zh": "急诊部门", "note": "医院中处理紧急患者的部门"}, {"word": "指摘する", "pos": "verb", "zh": "指出、指摘", "note": "正式表达，常用于报道中"}, {"word": "公約", "pos": "noun", "zh": "承诺、公约", "note": "尤指政治选举中的承诺"}, {"word": "停滞", "pos": "noun", "zh": "停滞", "note": "表示没有进展"}, {"word": "紹介", "pos": "noun", "zh": "转诊、介绍", "note": "医疗语境中指医生将患者转给专科"}, {"word": "割合", "pos": "noun", "zh": "比例", "note": "常与「～％」搭配"}, {"word": "上る", "pos": "verb", "zh": "达到、上升", "note": "此处表示数量达到某个程度"}, {"word": "懸念材料", "pos": "noun", "zh": "令人担忧的因素", "note": "正式表达，指引起担忧的事项"}], "title_original": "'Ominous signs' of winter pressures as NHS waiting list grows", "summary_original": "NHS winter pressures appear to be building already, with rises in waiting times for planned surgery.", "body_original": "'Ominous signs' of winter pressures as NHS waiting list grows\nBy\nDominic Hughes\nHealth correspondent\nPublished\n8 October 2026\nThere are \"ominous signs\" that winter pressures are already affecting the NHS in England, according to senior health leaders.\nThe warning comes as new data reveals the waiting list for routine hospital treatment in England rose for the second month in a row.\nAn estimated 7.37 million treatments were waiting to be carried out at the end of August, relating to 6.24 million patients.\nThe numbers are the highest since October 2025 and have raised questions over whether the NHS will meet a government target of treating 92% of patients within 18 weeks by 2029.\nThe rise in waiting lists comes despite the NHS in England delivering what were described as record levels of planned, elective care over the summer, while demand for services also reached its highest level ever.\nA record 4.7 million planned treatments, procedures and appointments occurred across June, July and August – more than in any previous summer.\nBut both A&Es and ambulance services also saw a record number of patients for the month of September.\nNHS England's national medical director, Professor Frankie Swords, warned that despite the progress delivered by frontline teams, winter pressure was already building.\n\"Staff are already seeing the ominous early signs of pressure, with more patients coming to A&E with flu and other respiratory viruses than usual for this time of year, and unfortunately many people are still waiting longer than we would like them to,\" she said.\nHealth and Social Care Secretary, Yvette Cooper said the NHS has been dealing with summer pressures as well as winter pressures.\n\"It is a huge tribute to doctors, nurses and staff across the NHS that alongside dealing with unprecedented levels of A&E attendances and ambulance call-outs, they also managed to deliver record numbers of elective appointments, procedures and treatments.\n\"Step by step, our NHS has been increasing its delivery and performance, making a real difference to patients' lives even as demand is growing.\n\"But with winter now approaching, pressure on our NHS is set to increase again and I would encourage everyone who is eligible for the flu jab and other vaccines to get themselves protected against preventable illnesses, and help relieve the workload on the NHS too.\"\n\"Relentless growth in demand for care\"\nThe NHS Alliance, which represents hospitals, says the government in England is not going to achieve its manifesto promise of hitting the 18-week hospital waiting time target by the end of the parliament in 2029.\nThat 18-week target hasn't been hit for a decade.\nA separate analysis by the Health Foundation think-tank said progress on cutting waiting times had stalled over the past year, with referrals on to the waiting list rising at a much quicker rate than the number of patients being treated.\nSir Ciarán Devane, the chief executive of the NHS Alliance which represents NHS trusts, said: \"The NHS continues to respond to record demand for care, but the relentless growth in demand for services is putting NHS staff under real pressure.\"\nFrancesca Cavallaro, of the Health Foundation, said: \"Thanks to the hard work of staff, the NHS has made progress in bringing down waiting times, but a rise in referrals mean that the service is having to run faster just to stand still and the prospects of meeting the government's pledge are receding.\n\"Andy Burnham's government have yet to set out whether they will give the 18-week target the same priority as it had under Keir Starmer, but our analysis shows the pledge is becoming increasingly hard to deliver.\"\n\"Not just numbers, but vulnerable people\"\nThere will be concern too that the pressures of a long, hot summer have merged almost seamlessly into the pressures associated with the winter months.\nMore patients, including children, have been arriving at A&E departments with flu and other respiratory viruses.\nThe number of patients seen within four hours in A&Es last month fell to 74.4%, down from 75.0% in August.\nThe number of people waiting more than 12 hours in A&E departments from a decision to admit to actually being admitted – what is known as \"corridor care\" – stood at 50,582 in September, up from 44,951 in August.\nThat has alarmed Dr Vicky Price, president of the Society for Acute Medicine.\n\"A 13% year-on-year rise in 12-hour emergency department waits as winter approaches should set alarm bells ringing.\n\"More than 50,000 patients waited over 12 hours from the decision to admit to admission in September - 1,686 people every day.\n\"These are not just numbers.\n\"They represent vulnerable people who are waiting far too long for a bed and staff trying to deliver safe care in overcrowded emergency departments.\"\nThe government says the 18-week mark could still be achieved, saying it was investing in NHS buildings and equipment to make services more productive.\nIt also pointed to disruption to care that was caused by the strikes by resident doctors, a dispute which has now been settled.\nBut the strain that services are feeling in September, before winter has even really got going, will be a cause for concern among NHS leaders and their political bosses alike.\nGet in touch\nHave you been on an NHS waiting list for a long time? Share your experience\nContact form\nContact form\nRelated topics\nNHS\nEngland\nHealth\nNHS England\nWaiting times\nMore on this story\nRise in people waiting for NHS treatment for fourth month in a row\nPublished\n17 September\nFears of two-tier health system as more turn to private care, says watchdog\nPublished\n16 March\nI'm on six different NHS waiting lists - it's taking over my life\nPublished\n23 April", "fetched_at": "2026-10-10T01:07:16.505883", "timeline": [{"i": 0, "w": "8", "s": 0.125, "e": 0.412, "sm": 125, "em": 412, "cs": 0, "ce": 1, "si": 0}, {"i": 1, "w": "月", "s": 0.412, "e": 0.7, "sm": 412, "em": 700, "cs": 1, "ce": 2, "si": 0}, {"i": 2, "w": "末", "s": 0.713, "e": 0.975, "sm": 712, "em": 975, "cs": 2, "ce": 3, "si": 0}, {"i": 3, "w": "時点", "s": 0.988, "e": 1.35, "sm": 987, "em": 1350, "cs": 3, "ce": 5, "si": 0}, {"i": 4, "w": "で", "s": 1.363, "e": 1.6, "sm": 1362, "em": 1600, "cs": 5, "ce": 6, "si": 0}, {"i": 5, "w": "、", "s": 1.6, "e": 1.788, "sm": 1600, "em": 1787, "cs": 6, "ce": 7, "si": 0}, {"i": 6, "w": "624", "s": 1.788, "e": 2.718, "sm": 1787, "em": 2717, "cs": 7, "ce": 10, "si": 0}, {"i": 7, "w": "万人", "s": 2.718, "e": 3.338, "sm": 2717, "em": 3337, "cs": 10, "ce": 12, "si": 0}, {"i": 8, "w": "の", "s": 3.35, "e": 3.462, "sm": 3350, "em": 3462, "cs": 12, "ce": 13, "si": 0}, {"i": 9, "w": "患者", "s": 3.475, "e": 3.8, "sm": 3475, "em": 3800, "cs": 13, "ce": 15, "si": 0}, {"i": 10, "w": "に", "s": 3.812, "e": 3.95, "sm": 3812, "em": 3950, "cs": 15, "ce": 16, "si": 0}, {"i": 11, "w": "関わる", "s": 3.962, "e": 4.425, "sm": 3962, "em": 4425, "cs": 16, "ce": 19, "si": 0}, {"i": 12, "w": "737", "s": 4.438, "e": 5.412, "sm": 4437, "em": 5412, "cs": 19, "ce": 22, "si": 0}, {"i": 13, "w": "万件", "s": 5.412, "e": 6.062, "sm": 5412, "em": 6062, "cs": 22, "ce": 24, "si": 0}, {"i": 14, "w": "の", "s": 6.075, "e": 6.175, "sm": 6075, "em": 6175, "cs": 24, "ce": 25, "si": 0}, {"i": 15, "w": "治療", "s": 6.188, "e": 6.612, "sm": 6187, "em": 